course: dictionary
lesson: 8885
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Showing is a word with more than one meaning. Its most common meaning is being seen. In «Alligators have wide U-shaped snouts that hide their lower teeth», the teeth are hidden, so showing is the opposite: something you can see.
explain: Read the words around it to choose the right meaning. «One event is often shown many times on different channels and phones» is about screens, so a showing here is a time when something is shown. Ask: what would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence to check it.
explain: Showing can also be a noun, a thing that happens at a time, like «a showing at 7». The spelling is the same, but it names an event, not an action. Look at how the word is used in the sentence to tell which job it is doing.
fact: Showing is the present participle of show: show, shows, showed, shown, showing.
fact: «Showing» means letting someone see something, or being seen.
fact: As a noun, «a showing» means a time when a film or performance is shown.
fact: «A good showing in the race» means a good result.
fact: «Showing» can also be a gentle, everyday way to say that a pregnancy can be seen.
exercise: «Crocodiles have V-shaped snouts with a big lower tooth showing.» What does showing mean here? | Broken off | Hidden away | Shouting loudly | *Able to be seen
exercise: «The film has a showing at 7.» What is a showing here? | A kind of animal | Mud on a path | *A time when the film is shown | A place to park a car
exercise: «She had a good showing in the race.» What does showing mean? | A bright light | Running very slowly | *A good result | A new pair of shoes
test: «Their eyes, ears and nostrils sit on top of the head, so a crocodile can lie in a river with only those showing.» What does showing mean here? | Able to be smelled | Able to be touched | *Able to be seen | Able to be heard
test: «One event is often shown many times; ten showings of a bombed building are still one building.» In this sentence, what is a showing? | A way of cooking food | Something that is hard to see | A building that is still standing | *A time when the event is shown on a screen
exam: Which meaning of showing fits «Only the eyes are showing above the water»? | Playing a film | A bad result | *Able to be seen | Hiding from view
